<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Summon Devil</h1>
<p>Sphere: Summoning Sphere
Class: Conjurer (guild level 50)
Mana: 40
</p><p>Usage:
</p>
<pre><a cmd='#'>cast summon devil</a>
tell devil &lt;command&gt;
</pre>
<p>The ultimate in summoning: a portal of fire opens, and a greater devil (level 
90) emerges to serve you. It follows you, fights beside you when you are in a 
fight, and when your hit points drop below a third it tries to rescue you. 
Like all summoned servants, it stays only a short time, from half a minute to 
a minute and a half. You can give it orders with tell: to attack (tell devil 
kill orc), to walk, and the like. It won't attack another player unless both 
of you have signed the Book of Blood. You can have only one summoned servant 
at a time: summoning another sends the first one away.
</p><p>Beware: if the spell fails, the devil steps through free, glad to be here 
unbound, and attacks you. At level 90, that is a fight few can survive. Even 
unbound, it goes back after a while, the longer the worse the spell 
failed, and banish can send it back sooner (see <a cmd='#'>Help Banish</a>).
</p><p>You must be standing, not fighting. It is also found on scrolls.
</p><p><br />
See Also:
</p>
<pre>&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Summon Demon</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Summoning Sphere</a>
</pre>




</div>